OILIF reproduction code and selected experiment archives

Architectures and source provenance:

* SDTv3 / E-SpikeFormer: adapted from the user's HARDVS experiment fork of
  BICLab/Spike-Driven-Transformer-V3.
  https://github.com/BICLab/Spike-Driven-Transformer-V3
  Only the 19M HARDVS architecture is retained. Upstream notices and terms
  continue to apply to third-party portions; this release does not assign
  a new license to the upstream project.

* SpikingJelly: the spiking ResNet34 architecture and neuron conventions
  are adapted from clock_driven/model/spiking_resnet.py and neuron.py.
  https://github.com/fangwei123456/spikingjelly
  Retained license: LICENSE-SPIKINGJELLY.

* Ultralytics / SpikeYOLO: detection blocks, loss, task-aligned assignment,
  box operations and AP evaluation are adapted from the experimental
  Ultralytics 8.0.197 fork. These sources retain AGPL-3.0 terms.
  https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics
  Retained license: LICENSE and object_detection/LICENSE.

* Prophesee event format: object_detection/prepare.py follows the Apache-2.0
  DAT format documented by the Prophesee automotive dataset toolbox.
  Copyright (c) Prophesee S.A. Retained license: LICENSE-APACHE-2.0.

* SHD/SSC preprocessing follows the historical experiment representation.
  Raw data are obtained separately from https://zenkelab.org/resources/.

New standalone glue code is covered by the root AGPL-3.0 license, subject to
retained third-party terms above. Dataset licenses are separate. The two
archived checkpoints documented in weights.json are the user's original
experiments; their metadata and hashes are retained for provenance. Model
weights, datasets and tracking exports are not included in this repository.
